<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lady Six Sky</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 741</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Lady Wak Chanil Ajaw</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lady Six Sky was a princess of Dos Pilas who arrived at Naranjo in 682 CE and restored its royal dynasty after defeats by Caracol. She governed for her young son K'ak' Tiliw Chan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaac">Chaak</a> and was shown on monuments in the guise of a warrior ruler. Her rule revived Naranjo as a regional power in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peten">Petén</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lady-six-sky.jpg" alt="Lady Six Sky" width="320" height="695" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MA_D367_Maya_stela_24,_Naranjo,_Guatemala.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
